    <string name="autostart_title">Autostart</string>
    <string name="autostart_description">Some phones block reminders when this app is not running. On OPPO / ColorOS, check Settings → Apps → Auto launch. This is separate from battery and background activity settings. This app cannot read or change the autostart switch; opening a screen does not mean it is enabled.</string>
    <string name="autostart_open">Open autostart settings</string>
    <string name="autostart_guide_title">Set up autostart manually</string>
    <string name="autostart_guide_unavailable">A direct link to autostart settings is not available on this phone. Follow the steps below instead.</string>
    <string name="autostart_guide_coloros">On OPPO / ColorOS, open Settings → Apps → Auto launch. Find %1$s and allow it to start automatically. The path may vary by system version; if needed, search Settings for “Auto launch” or “Autostart”.</string>
    <string name="autostart_guide_other_phones">On other phones, search system settings for “Autostart” or “App launch”. Menu names and availability vary by manufacturer.</string>
    <string name="autostart_guide_background_separate">App info is not the autostart entry. Battery and background activity controls are separate; allowing background activity does not mean autostart is enabled.</string>
    <string name="autostart_guide_navigation_only">The button below opens general system Settings, not the autostart screen. This app cannot read or change the autostart switch. Check it yourself, then return to this guide.</string>
